      "citation_ok": true,
      "auto_correct": true,
      "correct": true,
      "source": "manual",
      "rationale": "Confirms the automatic rule. The names COIR/M3GQA appear only in the Sources block, but the question asks which paper is the code one vs. the graph one and how many tasks/settings each defines: the body correctly assigns six settings to the graph benchmark and eight sub-tasks to the code benchmark, states nothing false (it says the main-task count is not stated rather than guessing), and both gold papers are cited."
